  ○ [p1_backend] Build FastAPI Backend
    agent:  Backend Developer (programmer_1)
    desc:   Create a complete FastAPI backend for a personal finance management app at /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_004/backend.

1. Create requirements.txt with: fastapi, uvicorn, sqlalchemy, python-dateutil, pydantic
2. Create a Python virtual environment named 'venv' inside the backend folder
3. Create main.py with FastAPI app, CORS middleware (allow all origins for dev)
4. Create database.py with SQLite setup via SQLAlchemy
5. Create models.py with:
   - Category model (id, name, type: 'income'|'expense', parent_id nullable for hierarchy)
   - Transaction model (id, category_id FK, amount float, date string, note text)
   - Budget model (id, category_id FK unique, month string 'YYYY-MM', amount float)
6. Create schemas.py with Pydantic models for request/response
7. Create seed.py that pre-populates categories:
   - Income (收入) with no children
   - Expense (支出) with children: 餐饮, 交通, 购物, 娱乐, 居住, 医疗, 教育, 其他
8. Create routers/categories.py (CRUD), routers/transactions.py (CRUD + filter by month + pagination), routers/budgets.py (CRUD + check budget status), routers/dashboard.py (monthly summary, expense by category for pie chart, 6-month trend)
9. Run seed.py to populate DB on startup

The backend should run on port 8000 with: uvicorn main:app --reload

IMPORTANT: Use 'project_dir' = '/Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_004/backend' so you know where to output files. When creating venv, create it INSIDE backend/venv. The startup script should also install requirements.
  ○ [p2_frontend] Build Next.js Frontend
    agent:  Frontend Developer (programmer_2)
    desc:   Create a complete Next.js (App Router) frontend for a personal finance management app at /Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_004/frontend.

Backend API runs at http://localhost:8000

1. Initialize with: npx create-next-app@latest . --typescript --tailwind --eslint --app --src-dir (in the frontend dir, with --use-npm). Then install shadcn/ui: npx shadcn@latest init -d --force. Then install recharts, lucide-react, and any other deps needed.

2. Create a lib/api.ts for all API calls:
   - Categories: fetchCategories, createCategory, updateCategory, deleteCategory
   - Transactions: fetchTransactions (with month filter, pagination), createTransaction, updateTransaction, deleteTransaction
   - Dashboard: fetchMonthlySummary (month), fetchTrend (6 months)
   - Budgets: fetchBudgets, createBudget, updateBudget, deleteBudget, fetchBudgetAlerts

3. Create components (use Shadcn UI components):
   - components/category-manager.tsx: CRUD table for categories, tree view with income/expense groups
   - components/transaction-form.tsx: Form dialog for adding/editing transactions (category dropdown, amount, date picker, note)
   - components/transaction-list.tsx: Table with pagination, month filter dropdown, edit/delete actions
   - components/monthly-summary.tsx: 3 cards showing total income, total expense, balance for current month
   - components/expense-pie-chart.tsx: Pie chart (Recharts) showing expense by category for current month
   - components/trend-chart.tsx: Line chart (Recharts) showing income/expense trends over last 6 months
   - components/budget-manager.tsx: Table showing each expense category's budget vs actual spending with progress bars; over-budget in red with warning icon

4. Create pages:
   - app/page.tsx (or app/dashboard/page.tsx): Main dashboard with monthly-summary, expense-pie-chart, trend-chart
   - app/transactions/page.tsx: Transaction list + form
   - app/categories/page.tsx: Category manager
   - app/budgets/page.tsx: Budget manager
   - app/layout.tsx: Sidebar navigation with links to Dashboard, Transactions, Categories, Budgets

IMPORTANT: Use 'project_dir' = '/Users/shenweizhang/Desktop/ai/run_test_004/frontend'. Make sure to install shadcn components like: button, card, dialog, input, select, table, label, separator, badge, progress. Use 'npx shadcn@latest add button card dialog input select table label separator badge progress -y' to add them.
